From 3f26f64a9816107c9fdeea75a5f9a96cf7abd92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huangserva <huangserva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:38:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] perf(sm70/tp2): faster decode round (attention, mailbox
 all-reduce, sharded heads)

- small-T int8 attention (v2): P x V accumulates in fp32 straight from the
  mma (drops 8 cvt + 8 FADD per fragment) and interior tiles load with
  page-base + constant offsets. 12/2 T=4 at 186K 662 -> 601 us; 24/4
  single card 1402 -> 1260 us.
- TP2 all-reduce for <= 128 KB goes through mapped pinned host memory
  (/dev/shm, cudaHostRegister) with per-CTA flags and step counters, rank-
  ordered fp32 sums so both ranks stay bit-identical; 40 KB 26 -> 16 us.
  Self-checked at init, 60 s spin timeout traps, NINFER_TP_MAILBOX=0 = NCCL.
- Output head (FP8, 248320 rows) and draft head (Q4, 131072 rows) are
  computed vocabulary-sharded and row-gathered through the mailbox; greedy
  output identical to the replicated heads. NINFER_TP_SHARD_HEADS=0 off.
- NVFP4 QPN prepacked kernel issues 8 groups of loads before decoding
  (bit-identical results): TP2 down 58.4 -> 54.5 us, gate/up half 47.9 ->
  43.6 us.

TP2 e2e: 186K code 86.7 -> 95.5 tok/s, 193K zh 67.0 -> 71.7 (per round
37.9 -> 33.1 ms), 8K code 121.0 -> 136.9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
